     The last two nothing else can say, and the loader has always
     done both silently - after which the load ORDER decides
     which stencil a drawing gets.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
                  velcheck amp1.d amp2.d
                  velcheck -sym pid.sym
                  velcheck -sym /usr/vellum/sym/*.sym

     The second form is the gate in /usr/vellum/etc/library.mk,
     so a wrong stencil never reaches a drawing.  The third finds
     the cross-library duplicate (``code R defined in both dis-
     crete.sym and power.sym'') that no single file can produce.

